  "compiled_abi": {
    "String": "Single pointer String return in this binary; native FromUtf8 receives span pointer/length in x0/x1 and returns StringImpl in x0. Actual Chromium String destructor releases it.",
    "EditorCommand": "24 bytes: internal command pointer at 0, source int at 8, frame pointer at 16. Source 0 is menu/key binding, as in the compiled native keyboard dispatch call site. Real InternalCommand lookup and EditorCommand::Execute preserve command beforeinput and validation.",
    "LocalFrame": "Existing decoded document/window/frame chain; compressed Editor member at +588 and EventHandler member at +592, verified by compiled Editor::HandleKeyboardEvent.",
    "selection": "Real TextControlElement selection start/end and SetSelectionRange. Native proposed delete range is applied in actual static TypingCommand delete entry points after beforeinput, only when canonical value and original selection remain unchanged.",
    "painting": "Existing ThemePainterDefault text-field rectangle and canvas. Prepared actual native bitmap replaces complete field; existing child-paint boundaries suppress anonymous text and guarded PaintCaretsIfNeeded suppresses the engine caret only for owned native fields.",
    "MouseEventWithHitTestResults": "EventWithHitTestResults embeds WebMouseEvent first. Its compiled InnerNode access decodes the signed compressed Member at +204; scrollbar is +236. WebMouseEvent button is +120 and click_count +160. SelectionController::HandleMousePressEvent disassembly confirms each access. Existing real coordinate conversion maps the engine event into native bitmap coordinates without glyph hit testing.",
    "pointer_lifecycle": "Real engine focus and cancellable pointer/mousedown dispatch precede SelectionController::HandleMousePressEvent. MouseEventManager retains press bookkeeping; native tracking owns character selection. Its drag-default entry bypasses engine data dragging and selection autoscroll during the claimed gesture. Selection release is suppressed only for that controller. The outer EventHandler::HandleMouseReleaseEvent restores bookkeeping even when mouseup is cancelled. Compiled drag manager frame Member at +0 matches the actual focused field frame.",
    "busy_editor": "Native op18 reads actual editor value, UTF-16 range, editability and focus. While tracking, op5 draws the busy actual editor without model/configuration changes. Canonical value/range, enabled/read-only, focus or dimensions changing ends tracking before rebinding. The eventfd work-loop callback echoes actual selection only while its canonical engine model remains unchanged."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Blink Editor key insertion uses actual DispatchBeforeInputInsertText then EventHandler::HandleTextInputEvent; using that same path retains text filtering, maxlength, trusted input, cancellation and undo.",
    "Editor::ExecuteCommand convenience aliases DeleteBackward to legacy BackwardDelete, which omits the expected beforeinput path. Resolve and execute the actual menu/key EditorCommand instead.",
    "Chromium WebKeyboardEvent text for Control+A can be a control character. Native logical shortcut input must use DOM key identity with modifiers; otherwise GNUstep cannot match its real Emacs binding. Printable input remains on keypress, after page cancellation.",
    "Native Return is dispatched on keypress only; keydown must retain the engine path that defers text-insertion commands.",
    "Cached field background snapshots require invalidation when the real engine updates inner editor values or selection. Real TextControlElement update/selection boundaries invalidate the owning layout rather than fabricating DOM changes.",
    "Actual native caret invalidations reuse the existing eventfd/work-loop integration. Helper loss also invalidates every native text field so original complete engine drawing returns immediately.",
    "Beforeinput/input removal/replacement cases pass. Native controls, rendering, caret timer and key bindings remain in the unchanged shared UI library.",
    "A shared input default handler also receives mouse events. Ending tracking before checking actual keydown/keypress type prematurely released native selection on mousemove. Modifier-only key events also preserve the active pointer gesture.",
    "Direct independent native references match all fifty Chromium click, Shift-click, forward/reverse and outside-field drag ranges. The bridge only transports coordinates and selection; actual NSTextField/NSSecureTextField mouseDown owns hit testing and tracking.",
    "The installed agent-browser mouse CLI accepts integer coordinates and cannot hold Shift across mouse input. The pointer checker retains its owned session for page inspection/screenshots and uses the existing owned page CDP endpoint solely for fractional/modified pointer input, via Node built-in WebSocket. No alternate browser driver or package install is required."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Multiple-click metadata, dragging selected text as data, context menus, touch and long-field horizontal/autoscroll behavior for Chromium fields.",
    "Clipboard web events and native cut/paste/undo command routing, typing undo grouping, selection-event/direction semantics, IME/composition and accessibility.",
    "Native intrinsic sizing, other text types, multiline/rich text, broad author styling, transforms and non-1 scale output.",
    "Cached-page lifecycle, long validators/modal editing flows, other Chromium builds/derivatives and browser address bars/frontends.",
    "Complete Firefox frontends and remaining GTK/Qt/KDE application surfaces."
  ]
}
